<title>BELGIUM: EU rice experts to discuss compensatory aid.</title>
<headline>EU rice experts to discuss compensatory aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's rice management committee will discuss on Thursday detailed rules on compensatory aid for rice producers, an EU official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Under the reform of the rice regime there is to be a gradual reduction in the intervention price for rice. EU producers will get area compensatory payments similar to those which apply in the cereals sector,&quot; the offcial said.</p>
<p>The first area payments are due to be issued for the 1997/98 marketing year next year. No formal decision is expected at Thursday's meeting of the Cereals and Rice Management Committee.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
